STAGE-1 EXPEDIENT: build zstd with its own upstream Makefile instead of cmake,
so that `cmd:cmake` is not needed at all.

This is what actually freed `zstd` and, behind it, `openssl3`. It replaced a much
more ambitious attempt to build cmake itself, which failed (see
cmake-4.1.6-bundled-libs-stage1.patch and Blocker 6 in
graviton/docs/package-chain-status.md).

## Why cmake was the blocker

`zstd-1.5.6.recipe:102` lists `cmd:cmake` in BUILD_PREREQUIRES, and cmake sits in
a four-node link cycle:

    cmake -> devel:libcurl -> openssl3 -> devel:libzstd -> zstd -> cmd:cmake

Note the status doc previously recorded zstd as "blocked on xz_utils
(devel:liblzma)". liblzma was real but it was not the binding constraint —
`cmd:cmake` was, and satisfying liblzma alone would never have freed zstd.

## Why the Makefile route is a small sacrifice

zstd's `Makefile` / `lib/Makefile` / `programs/Makefile` are a first-class,
upstream-maintained build path, not a legacy fallback. The build log confirms the
result is equivalent where it matters:

    compiling multi-threaded dynamic library 1.5.6
    creating versioned links
    release build completed
    ==> building with threading support
    ==> building zstd with .gz compression support
    ==> building zstd with .xz/.lzma compression support
    ==> building zstd with .lz4 compression support

Same `libzstd.so.1.5.6` with soname `libzstd.so.1`, same headers, same
`libzstd.pc`, and the CLI picked up gz/xz/lz4 support — including the liblzma from
the `xz_utils` built earlier in this same chain.

**What is lost:** the CMake package-config files
(`lib/cmake/zstd/zstdTargets*.cmake`, and the recipe's `fixCMake` + two `sed`
fixups that rewrite them). Consumers using `find_package(zstd CONFIG)` will not
find it; `pkg-config --libs libzstd` still works, and that is what autotools
consumers — including openssl3 — actually use. Restore the cmake `BUILD()`/
`INSTALL()` verbatim once `cmd:cmake` exists.

## Two traps this hit, both of the "read the actual Makefile" kind

1. **`contrib/pzstd` died with `Error 127`.**

       aarch64-unknown-haiku-g++ ... -c main.cpp -o main.o
       make: aarch64-unknown-haiku-g++: No such file or directory

   `contrib/pzstd/Makefile` uses `$(CXX)`, which haikuporter sets to the triplet
   name. That binary *does* exist (`/boot/system/develop/tools/bin/`) but is not on
   the sub-make's PATH, so it fails while `lib/` and `programs/` — which had
   already completed — used plain `cc`. Fixed with `CXX=g++`. Same family as the
   `aclocal-1.17` failure in libtool: a tool name baked into a Makefile that does
   not exist under that name here.

2. **`MANDIR=` is silently ignored; the variable is `MAN1DIR`.** From
   `programs/Makefile`:

       389:  man1dir     ?= $(mandir)/man1
       393:    MAN1DIR ?= $(MANDIR)/man1      # BSD branch only
       395:    MAN1DIR ?= $(man1dir)          # <- Haiku takes this one

   Only the BSD branch derives `MAN1DIR` from `MANDIR`, so on Haiku a `MANDIR=`
   override does nothing and the pages land in `$prefix/share/man/man1`. The
   failure surfaced far away, in `packageEntries`:

       mv: cannot stat '/packages/zstd-1.5.6-2/.self/documentation/man/man1'

   Passing `MAN1DIR=$manDir/man1` is correct and works on both branches.
   `PKGCONFIGDIR` is deliberately *not* overridden — the default
   `$(libdir)/pkgconfig` is where `fixPkgconfig` expects it, matching every
   autotools port here.

Applies to: input-source-packages/develop/sources/zstd-1.5.6-2/zstd-1.5.6.recipe

--- a/zstd-1.5.6.recipe
+++ b/zstd-1.5.6.recipe
@@ BUILD_PREREQUIRES
 	cmd:gcc$secondaryArchSuffix
-	cmd:cmake
+#	cmd:cmake	# graviton: built with zstd's own Makefile instead
 	cmd:make
 	cmd:sed
 	cmd:find
@@ BUILD() / INSTALL()
+# STAGE-1 NOTE (graviton): built with zstd's OWN upstream Makefile instead of
+# cmake. cmd:cmake is the edge that keeps zstd inside the link cycle
+# cmake -> libcurl -> openssl3 -> libzstd -> zstd -> cmd:cmake, and no cmake
+# exists natively yet. zstd's Makefile build is a fully supported upstream path
+# (lib/Makefile + programs/Makefile) and produces the same libzstd.so.1.5.6 with
+# soname libzstd.so.1, the same headers and the same libzstd.pc.
+# What is lost relative to the cmake build: the CMake package-config files
+# (lib/cmake/zstd/zstdTargets*.cmake), so find_package(zstd CONFIG) will not
+# work for consumers -- pkg-config still does. Restore the cmake BUILD()/INSTALL()
+# once cmd:cmake exists.
 BUILD()
 {
-	cmake -B bld -S build/cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
-		$cmakeDirArgs \
-		-DCMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR=$commandBinDir \
-		-DZSTD_BUILD_STATIC=OFF \
-		-DZSTD_BUILD_TESTS=ON \
-		-DZSTD_PROGRAMS_LINK_SHARED=ON
-	make -C bld $jobArgs
+	make $jobArgs
+	# CXX=g++: contrib/pzstd/Makefile uses $(CXX), which haikuporter sets to the
+	# triplet name aarch64-unknown-haiku-g++ -- that binary is not on PATH in the
+	# chroot (only g++/c++ are), so pzstd died with 'No such file or directory'
+	# and Error 127 while lib/ and programs/ had already built fine.
+	make -C contrib/pzstd $jobArgs CXX=g++
 }

 INSTALL()
 {
-	make -C bld install
+	make install \
+		PREFIX=$prefix \
+		LIBDIR=$libDir \
+		INCLUDEDIR=$includeDir \
+		BINDIR=$commandBinDir \
+		MAN1DIR=$manDir/man1
+	# MAN1DIR, not MANDIR: programs/Makefile:389 has "man1dir ?= $(mandir)/man1"
+	# and :395 "MAN1DIR ?= $(man1dir)", and only the BSD branch (:393) derives
+	# MAN1DIR from MANDIR. Haiku takes the else branch, so a MANDIR= override is
+	# silently ignored and the pages land in $prefix/share/man/man1 -- which then
+	# broke packageEntries with "mv: cannot stat .../documentation/man/man1".
+	# pkgconfig is deliberately left at its default $(libdir)/pkgconfig, which is
+	# where fixPkgconfig expects it (same as every autotools port here).
+
+	# the Makefile build installs a static lib too; the recipe ships shared only
+	rm -f $libDir/libzstd.a
+
+	install -m 755 contrib/pzstd/pzstd $commandBinDir/pzstd

 	mkdir -p $docDir
 	cp doc/zstd_manual.html $docDir

 	prepareInstalledDevelLib libzstd
 	fixPkgconfig
-	fixCMake
-
-	sed "s|$libDir|$developLibDir|g" \
-		-i $developLibDir/cmake/zstd/zstdTargets-release.cmake
-	sed "/INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES/c INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES \"$includeDir;\"" \
-		-i $developLibDir/cmake/zstd/zstdTargets.cmake

 	packageEntries bin \
 		$commandBinDir
@@ TEST()
 TEST()
 {
-	make -C bld test
+	make test
 }
